<title>JAPAN: Japan April external reserves at record $219.9 bln.</title>
<headline>Japan April external reserves at record $219.9 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's external reserves rose $0.565 billion from a month earlier to a record $219.922 billion at the end of April, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The reserves at the end of March were $219.357 billion, the previous record, which was up $1.098 billion from the previous month.</p>
<p>Figures may not tally due to rounding.</p>
</text>
